ts{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-03T11:13:19Z","updated_at":"2026-08-03T11:13:33Z","body":"> Changing only the bone order can also cause issues.\n> \n>  ScreenRecording.mov \n> [spring_bone_simulator_3d 2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30658142/spring_bone_simulator_3d.2.zip)\n\nThis is expected behavior since renaming/reordering bones changes their index positions in the new skeleton, which breaks the parent-child relationship between the stored `root_bone` & `end_bone` indices. Since the hierarchy chain is no longer valid for those indices, the Editor flags it and clears the joints until the bones are re-selected in the Inspector.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5165599512/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5165889849","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122049#issuecomment-5165889849","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122049","id":5165889849,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM-k5OQ","user":{"login":"shanayyy","id":13399488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMzk5NDg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13399488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy","html_url":"https://github.com/shanayyy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shanayyy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-03T11:45:49Z","updated_at":"2026-08-03T11:45:49Z","body":"Since the settings already store the bone names for root_bone and end_bone, could we resolve the bone indices again from the new skeleton when the skeleton is changed? Currently, the correct indices can be assigned through a script after switching skeletons, but having errors printed to the console on every switch is not ideal.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5165889849/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]